      "title": "Chip holds quantum information for over a microsecond",
      "summary": "University of Illinois researchers stored quantum information carried by photons on a microchip for more than a microsecond. Quantum networks need this kind of pause so that slower operations can catch up with the light. A microsecond is still very short, and practical quantum networks need far longer storage and many connected devices.",
